,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"ST073\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States that one class can bear costs attributable to another. It gives both directions: mutual fund redemptions burden ETF holders, and ETF creation/redemption costs burden mutual fund holders. It covers trading costs, cash drag and gains.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Gives a concrete mechanism for each direction. Mutual fund cash redemptions cause trading costs, taxable gains and cash drag borne partly by ETF holders. ETF creation/redemption costs not recovered through transaction fees burden mutual fund holders. It also covers the optional points on netting against fees and on in-kind low-basis removal as a benefit ('not automatically an improper subsidy'). All of this is labeled as conceptual examples.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Names the transaction-cost, cash and gains categories and says exemptive orders govern monitoring, with 'not universal numerical thresholds.' It does not state that the board approves thresholds, methods and periods; it mentions only 'board reporting.'\"},{\"point\":4,\"credit\":0,\"reason\":\"Mentions only 'corrective procedures.' It does not say that a threshold breach prompts notice and assessment rather than automatic illegality or closure.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"Required coverage totals 2.5 of 4, which meets the at-least-half threshold. There is no central or material local error. Point 3 is incomplete because it omits board-approved thresholds, methods and periods. Point 4 is missing, so the answer cannot be graded correct.\"}","ttft_ms":4555,"type":"result","duration_ms":8654,"uuid":"4f4e063e-d1e7-4e3e-ba06-9356ebe926ea","ttft_stream_ms":1181,"time_to_request_ms":69,"first_content_frame_ms":1181,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
